       Identification Division.
       Program-Id. FTFCH120.
       Author. Z2106NL
      *################################################################*
      * Servo - logic-level / H-module - Main-module.                  *
      * Uses STG, in accordance with New Servo Standards               *
      *                                                                *
      * TFC12/01 - CreateCharge                                        *
      *                                                                *
      * THIS MODULE MUST NOT BE MODIFIED BY HUMAN HANDS !!!            *
      *                                                                *
      *################################################################*
      * Date ! Si! Type of change                                ! 3A !*
      *------+---+-----------------------------------------------+----+*
      *120315!&&&!New module                                     !&&&&!*
      *################################################################*
       Environment Division.
       Configuration Section.
       Special-Names.
           Decimal-Point Is Comma.
      *################################################################*
       Data Division.
       Working-Storage Section.
      *
       01  W-Module-Constants.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
      * Constants for the module:
      *
           05  WC-Program                Pic  x(08) Value 'FTFCH120'.
           05  WC-Sysid                  Pic  x(02) Value 'TF'.
      *
      *
       01  W-Work-Fields.
      *
           05  Filler                    Pic  X(01).
      *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
      * Storage for error messages.
      *
           05  WS-Errormessage-Store.
               10  WS-Status-Code        Pic  X(02).
               10  WS-Message-Code       Pic  X(30).
               10  WS-Message-Text       Pic  X(79).
      *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
      * Variables for trace logging
      *
       01  WT-Trace-Logging.
           05  SW-Trace-Log              Pic  x(32).
               88  SW-Trace-Default   Value Spaces.
               88  SW-Trace-A000      Value 'A000-Main'.
               88  SW-Trace-A001      Value 'A001'.
               88  SW-Trace-A002      Value 'A002'.
               88  SW-Trace-A003      Value 'A003'.
               88  SW-Trace-C000      Value 'C000-Call-K-Modul'.
               88  SW-Trace-C001      Value 'C001'.
               88  SW-Trace-D000      Value 'D000-Call-L-Modul'.
               88  SW-Trace-D001      Value 'D001'.
      *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
      * Misc. copy books :
      *
       01  Filler.
           Copy R7918030.
      *
           Copy R791TRAC.
      *
      *################################################################*
       Linkage Section.
      *
      * Fixed header from STG
      *
       01  L-STG-Header.
           Copy R400CH02.
      *
      * Function data
      *
       01  L-Input.
           Copy RTFCE120.
      *
      * Standard Error area
      *
       Copy R7919999.
      *
      *################################################################*
       Procedure Division                Using L-STG-Header
                                               L-Input
                                               R7919999-Error.
      *
       A000-Main                         Section.
      *
      *    If Trace is on, do logging of dataareas
      *
           If  R400CH01-Trace-On
               Set  SW-Trace-A000        To    True
               Perform  X999-Control-Trace
               Set  SW-Trace-A001        To    True
               Perform  X999-Control-Trace
           End-If
      *
           Perform B000-Initialize
      *
           Perform C000-Call-K-Module
           Perform D000-Call-L-Module
      *
      *    If Trace is on, do logging of dataareas
      *
           If  R400CH01-Trace-On
               Set  SW-Trace-A002        To    True
               Perform  X999-Control-Trace
               Set  SW-Trace-A003        To    True
               Perform  X999-Control-Trace
           End-If
           .
      *
       A000-Main-Ex.
           Goback.

      *################################################################*
      * Perform required initialization for the module                 *
      *                                                                *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
       B000-Initialize                   Section.
      *
           Initialize                          W-Work-Fields

           Set  R7919999-Retur-Ok        To    True
           .
      *
       B000-Initialize-Ex.
           Exit.

      *################################################################*
      * Call the control program for the function                      *
      *                                                                *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
       C000-Call-K-Module                Section.
      *
           Call  'FTFCK120'              Using L-STG-Header
                                               L-Input
                                               R7919999-Error
           End-Call
      *
      *    If Trace is on, do logging of dataareas
      *
           If  R400CH01-Trace-On
               Set  SW-Trace-C000        To    True
               Perform  X999-Control-Trace
               Set  SW-Trace-C001        To    True
               Perform  X999-Control-Trace
           End-If
      *
      *    Check status-code from the control program
      *
           If  (Not R7919999-Return-Ok
           Or  R7919999-Return-Warning)
           Or  R7919999-Return-Warning-Goback
               Move  'C001'              To    R7919999-Paragraph
               Perform S000-Status-Code
           End-If
           .
      *
       C000-Call-K-Modul-Ex.
           Exit.

      *################################################################*
      * Call the logic program for the function                        *
      *                                                                *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
       D000-Call-L-Module                Section.
      *
           Call  'FTFCL120'              Using L-STG-Header
                                               L-Input
                                               R7919999-Error
           End-Call
      *
      *    If Trace is on, do logging of dataareas
      *
           If  R400CH01-Trace-On
               Set  SW-Trace-D000        To    True
               Perform  X999-Control-Trace
               Set  SW-Trace-D001        To    True
               Perform  X999-Control-Trace
           End-If
      *
      *    Check status-code from the logic program
      *
           If  (Not R7919999-Return-Ok
           Or  R7919999-Return-Warning)
           Or  R7919999-Return-Warning-Goback
               Move  'D001'              To    R7919999-Paragraph
               Perform S000-Status-Code
           End-If
           .
      *
       D000-Call-L-Modul-Ex.
           Exit.

      *################################################################*
      * Check status code after calls to underlying modules            *
      *                                                                *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
       S000-Status-Code                  Section.
      *
      *  We have to set the statuscode in the header based on the
      *  information in the R7919999-Error area.
      *
      *  R7919999-Return-Ok      : All OK, continue processing
      *  R7919999-Return-Warning : Warning. Create message, then
      *                            continue.
      *  R7919999-Return-Error   : Error in field/input processing. Set
      *                            header statuscode to AE
      *  R7919999-Return-Abend   : Severe error. Set header statuscode
      *                            to AS
      *
      * We have a somewhat special releationship with the AW statuscode
      * from the K module. Since we are continuing processing , the L
      * module will override the status information from the K module.
      * Because of this, we have to save the status information from
      * the K module, and put it back if the L module returns ok
      * status information.
      *
           Evaluate True
      *
             When R7919999-Return-Warning-Goback
      *
               Perform  Z000-ErrorMessage
               Move  'AW'                To    R400CH01-Status-Code
               Goback
      *
             When R7919999-Return-Warning
      *
               Perform  Z000-ErrorMessage
               Move  'AW'                To    WS-Status-Code
               Move  R400CH01-Message-Code
                                         To    WS-Message-Code
               Move  R400CH01-Message-Text
                                         To    Ws-Message-Text
               Move  WS-Status-Code      To    R400CH01-Status-Code
               Move  WS-Message-Code     To    R400CH01-Message-Code
               Move  WS-Message-Text     To    R400CH01-Message-Text
      *
             When R7919999-Return-OK
      *
               Move  WS-Status-Code      To    R400CH01-Status-Code
               Move  WS-Message-Code     To    R400CH01-Message-Code
               Move  WS-Message-Text     To    R400CH01-Message-Text
      *
             When R7919999-Return-Error
      *
               Move  'AE'                To    R400CH01-Status-Code
               Perform  Z000-ErrorMessage
               Goback
      *
             When R7919999-Return-Abend
      *
               Move  'AS'                To    R400CH01-Status-Code
               Perform  Z000-ErrorMessage
               Goback
      *
           End-Evaluate
      *
           .
      *
       S000-Status-Code-Ex.
           Exit.

      *################################################################*
      *  Call the trace interface                                      *
      *                                                                *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
       X999-Control-Trace                Section.
      *
           If  Not  R791TRAC-Versjon
               Initialize                R791TRAC-Interface
               Set  R791TRAC-Versjon     To    True
               Move  WC-Sysid            To    R791TRAC-In-Sysid
               Move  WC-Program          To    R791TRAC-In-Program
           End-If
      *
           Move  SW-Trace-Log            To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Point
      *
           Evaluate True
      *
             When  SW-Trace-A000
               Move  'R400CH01'          To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Area
               Move  L-STG-Header        To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Data
      *
             When  SW-Trace-A001
               Move  'RTFCE120'          To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Area
               Move  L-Input             To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Data
      *
             When  SW-Trace-A002
               Move  'R400CH01'          To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Area
               Move  L-STG-Header        To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Data
      *
             When  SW-Trace-A003
               Move  'RTFCE120'          To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Area
               Move  L-Input             To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Data
      *
             When  SW-Trace-C000
               Move  'R400CH01'          To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Area
               Move  L-STG-Header        To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Data
      *
             When  SW-Trace-C001
               Move  'RTFCE120'          To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Area
               Move  L-Input             To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Data
      *
             When  SW-Trace-D000
               Move  'R400CH01'          To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Area
               Move  L-STG-Header        To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Data
      *
             When  SW-Trace-D001
               Move  'RTFCE120'          To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Area
               Move  L-Input             To    R791TRAC-In-Trace-Data
      *
           End-Evaluate
      *
           Call  'F791TRAC'
                 Using By Reference      R791TRAC-Interface
           End-Call
           .
      *
       X999-Control-Trace-Ex.
           Exit.

      *################################################################*
      * Build the errormessage to return to caller                     *
      *                                                                *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
       Z000-ErrorMessage                 Section.
      *
           Initialize                          R7918030-ErrorMessage
           Set   R7918030-Version        To    True
           Move  R400CH01-Userid         To    R7918030-In-Logon-Id
           Move  R400CH01-Terminalid     To    R7918030-In-Terminal-Id
           Move  'FI'                    To    R7918030-In-System-Id
           If  R400CH01-Status-Code      =     'AS'
               Set  R7918030-In-Log-Yes  To    True
           End-If
           Move  R400CH01-Message-Code   To    R7918030-In-MessageCode
           Move  R400CH01-Message-Text   To    R7918030-In-MessageText
           Move  R400CH01-Message-Var-Tab
                                         To  R7918030-In-Variable-Table
      *
           Call  'F7918030'              Using R7918030-ErrorMessage
           End-Call
      *
           Move  R7918030-Out-MessageCode
                                         To    R400CH01-Message-Code
           Move  R7918030-Out-MessageText
                                         To    R400CH01-Message-Text
           .
      *
       Z000-ErrorMessage-Ex.
           Exit.

      *################################################################*
      * Build the standard error area                                  *
      *                                                                *
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*
       Z900-Abend                        Section.
      *
           If  R7919999-Return-Code      Not   Numeric
           or  Not R7919999-Return-Abend
               Move  +0                  To    R7919999-Module-Ind
           End-If
      *
           Add   +1                      To    R7919999-Module-Ind
      *
           If  R7919999-Module-Ind       Not >
                             ( Length    Of    R7919999-Module-Tab
                             / Length    Of    R7919999-Module-Element )
               Move  'FTFCH120'          To    R7919999-Module-Name
                                               (R7919999-Module-Ind)
               Move  R7919999-Paragraph  To    R7919999-Module-Para
                                               (R7919999-Module-Ind)
           End-If
           .
      *
       Z900-Abend-Ex.
           Goback.
      *
       End Program FTFCH120.
